# 必考词 Unit03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit03核心高频词汇

{{background}}{/ˈbækɡraʊnd/}{{n. 背景；经历}}{{He has a strong background in computer science.}}

{{balance}}{/ˈbæləns/}}{n. 平衡；余额；v. 使平衡}}{{It is important to maintain a balance between work and life.}}

{{ban}}{/bæn/}{{v. 禁止；n. 禁令}}{{The government banned smoking in public places.}}

{{barrier}}{/ˈbæriər/}{{n. 障碍；屏障}}{{Language can be a barrier to effective communication.}}

{{basis}}{/ˈbeɪsɪs/}{{n. 基础；根据}}{{The theory was established on a solid basis of evidence.}}

{{behalf}}{/bɪˈhɑːf/}{{n. 代表；利益}}{{The lawyer spoke on behalf of his client.}}

{{behave}}{/bɪˈheɪv/}{{v. 表现；举止}}{{The children behaved well during the ceremony.}}

{{benefit}}{/ˈbenɪfɪt/}}{n. 利益；好处；v. 受益}}{{Regular exercise has many health benefits.}}

{{betray}}{/bɪˈtreɪ/}{{v. 背叛；泄露}}{{He would never betray his friends.}}

{{bias}}{/ˈbaɪəs/}}{n. 偏见；偏差}}{{The research aims to eliminate bias from the results.}}

{{bind}}{/baɪnd/}{{v. 捆绑；约束}}{{The contract binds both parties to the agreement.}}

{{blank}}{/blæŋk/}{{adj. 空白的；茫然的}}{{She stared at the blank page, unable to write anything.}}

{{blast}}{/blɑːst/}{{n. 爆炸；一阵（风）}}{{The blast destroyed several buildings in the area.}}

{{blend}}{/blend/}{{v. 混合；融合}}{{The artist blended different colors to create the painting.}}

{{block}}{/blɒk/}}{n. 街区；障碍物；v. 阻碍}}{{The fallen tree blocked the road completely.}}

{{boom}}{/buːm/}{{n./v. 繁荣；轰鸣}}{{The technology industry experienced a boom in the 1990s.}}

{{boost}}{/buːst/}}{v. 促进；提高}}{{The new policy will boost economic growth.}}

{{border}}{/ˈbɔːrdər/}{{n. 边界；边缘}}{{The two countries share a long border.}}

{{bound}}{/baʊnd/}{{adj. 必定的；受约束的}}{{He is bound to succeed with such dedication.}}

{{boundary}}{/ˈbaʊndri/}{{n. 边界；界限}}{{The river forms the boundary between the two regions.}}

{{branch}}{/brɑːntʃ/}}{n. 树枝；分支；部门}}{{The company has branches in many countries.}}

{{breach}}{/briːtʃ/}}{n. 违反；缺口；v. 违反}}{{The leak was a serious breach of security.}}

{{breed}}{/briːd/}{{v. 繁殖；培养；n. 品种}}{{Hardship breeds resilience in people.}}

{{brief}}{/briːf/}{{adj. 简短的；n. 摘要}}{{He gave a brief summary of the report.}}

{{brilliant}}{/ˈbrɪliənt/}{{adj. 辉煌的；杰出的}}{{She came up with a brilliant idea to solve the problem.}}

{{broadcast}}{/ˈbrɔːdkɑːst/}}{v. 广播；传播}}{{The event was broadcast live on national television.}}

{{budget}}{/ˈbʌdʒɪt/}}{n. 预算；v. 编预算}}{{The government increased the budget for healthcare.}}

{{bulk}}{/bʌlk/}}{n. 大量；大部分}}{{The bulk of the work has already been completed.}}

{{burden}}{/ˈbɜːrdn/}}{n. 负担；责任}}{{The tax burden on small businesses has increased.}}

{{burst}}{/bɜːrst/}{{v. 爆裂；突然发生}}{{The audience burst into applause after the performance.}}

{{campaign}}{/kæmˈpeɪn/}}{n. 运动；竞选活动}}{{The charity launched a campaign to raise awareness.}}

{{candidate}}{/ˈkændɪdət/}}{n. 候选人；应试者}}{{Five candidates applied for the manager position.}}

{{capable}}{/ˈkeɪpəbl/}{{adj. 有能力的；能干的}}{{She is capable of handling complex tasks efficiently.}}

{{capacity}}{/kəˈpæsəti/}}{n. 容量；能力}}{{The stadium has a capacity of 80,000 spectators.}}

{{capture}}{/ˈkæptʃər/}{{v. 捕获；夺取}}{{The photographer captured the beautiful sunset.}}

{{casual}}{/ˈkæʒuəl/}{{adj. 随意的；偶然的}}{{He made a casual remark that offended everyone.}}

{{category}}{/ˈkætəɡəri/}}{n. 类别；种类}}{{The books are divided into different categories.}}

{{cease}}{/siːs/}{{v. 停止；终止}}{{The factory ceased production due to lack of raw materials.}}

{{celebrate}}{/ˈselɪbreɪt/}{{v. 庆祝；赞美}}{{People gathered to celebrate the national holiday.}}

{{challenge}}{/ˈtʃælɪndʒ/}}{n. 挑战；v. 质疑}}{{Climate change is one of the greatest challenges of our time.}}
